    formula stacks with it. With `sdc_base` stated, no `men_of_arms` line.
  - M.D.C. IS NOT STORED AS `mdc_base`. The book''s M.D.C. line is the psionic
    force field (150 + 10 per level), which exists only while switched on for
    10 I.S.P.; it is a natural ability.
  - HIT POINTS: "P.E.x5, plus 2D6 per level of experience".
  - PSIONICS: master psionic. I.S.P. is M.E. plus 2D6x10, +10 per additional
    level. The book grants 1D4+1 Physical and 1D4 Super powers, rolled. The
    starting groups hold a number rather than dice, so each is stored at the
    MOST the roll can give (5 and 4, total 9), with a note telling the player
    to roll and take only that many. A judgement call. No powers are gained
    at later levels; the book states none. The force field and force blasts
    are the class''s own abilities, not catalog powers, and are natural
    abilities.
  - BONUSES stored: +2 initiative, +1 attack, +2 strike, parry and dodge, +4
    pull punch, +4 save vs horror factor, +2 vs psionics, +2 vs magic
    (`spell_magic`), and +30% vs coma/death (`coma_death_pct`, from item 2).
    The frenzy modifiers ("triple during frenzy", "gone during frenzy", +10
    P.S., +1 strike/parry/dodge) are conditional and in prose. Supernatural
    strength applies "in P.P.E. rich environments", so it is prose too.
    Horror Factor 12 is the top-level `horror_factor`.
  - Claws'' +10% to climb is prose: the class does not grant Climbing, so a
    player who takes it adds the 10% by hand.
  - SKILLS: Basic Math is `Mathematics: Basic` 45+10; Lore: Demons and
    Monsters is `Lore: Demons & Monsters` 25+10; Spanish 50+30; Ancient
    Egyptian has no catalog row and is a fixed `Language: Other` at 50+30 with
    the tongue in its note; the language of choice is a Language: Other pick
    at +10. Tracking: Humans and Monsters is `Tracking (people)` 25+20;
    Tracking: Animals is `Track & Trap Animals` 20+20; Land Navigation 36+10;
    Wilderness Survival 30+15; Prowl 25+15.
  - HAND TO HAND: the book grants "Martial Arts or Assassin (if evil)" and
    prints no upgrade price, so it is a choice of the two and there is no
    `hand_to_hand` block. The evil condition is in the note, not enforced.
  - RELATED: four, plus one at levels 3, 7, 11 and 15. Printed bonuses
    stored as category bonuses: Communications +5, Domestic +5, Espionage +5,
    Medical +5 (First Aid and Holistic Medicine only), Pilot +5, Rogue +6 (as
    printed; the render confirms 6), Technical +5, Wilderness +10.
    Electrical, Physical, Pilot Related and W.P. any, no bonus. Mechanical,
    Military and Science None, omitted. The book lists no Horsemanship or
    Cowboy category and neither is granted.
  - SECONDARY: four, plus two at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, from the same
    categories without bonuses, "excluding those marked None".
  - EQUIPMENT: "an energy rifle (equivalent to a Wilk''s laser rifle) or a
    Colombian rocket rifle" is a choice of `wilk-s-447-laser-rifle` and
    `rr-c40-rocket-rifle` (the Colombian rocket rifle of printed 23-24). The
    blade weapon of choice is enumerated as vibro-knife, vibro-saber,
    vibro-sword, machete and survival knife - a judgement call. "Heavy cat
    warrior armor (M.D.C. 90)" is `heavy-cat-warrior-armor`, a row
    add-south-america-felinoid-gear.sql adds;
    the book gives no stat block beyond the 90
    M.D.C. Survival kit is the existing `survival-kit`.
  - Money: 1D4X1000 credits in salable articles. Salable goods are not coin, so
    starting_money is not stored (as with the other Felinoids); it is a
    restriction line.
---

## Lore

The hunter cat was the crowning result of Argentina''s Achilles Project: a
felinoid built from tiger, jaguar, gorilla and human genes, with a healing
factor and muscle strength far beyond anything its makers expected. Some of
its gifts proved to be psionic, including a set of psychic super-powers that
let a bare-handed hunter cat match a human in power armor. The frightened
project director wanted them destroyed; the government refused.

The flaw was the killing instinct. Hunter cats live for the hunt and the kill,
and their blood lust too often overwhelms their reason. Since the Coming of
the Rifts their powers have grown stronger and their tempers shorter. Most
now serve Omagua faithfully as its protectors, but now and then one goes
berserk, and oracle cats are the city''s best means of calming them.

## GM Notes

Renegade hunter cats become murderers, bandit lords or feral monsters that
claim a territory of about 50 miles (80 km) and kill every trespasser, their
I.Q. halved. The worst are evil hunter cats who go rogue with their wits
intact, becoming assassins, warlords, or the partners of witches,
necromancers, vampires, demons and evil gods.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hunter-cat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hunter-cat';

